# The fork of Idris's compiler (compiler/idris) carries the change of
# upstream/53-constructor-implicit-mark/pull-request.diff, which also fixes
# upstream/54-erased-constant-pattern: at quantity 0, a constant or a type
# that a clause writes on an erased argument is a match of the definition's
# case tree, while what the clause leaves to unification is split after it
# and stays a variable unless it is a constructor, as does every part of it.
# Main.idr's `h 5` reduces to 2, which `hFive` and the type of `five` say,
# and `heads`, whose `All`'s implicit unification fixes to the pair its
# clause writes, is covering, the types in that pair being no match; the
# pinned, unpatched Idris takes `h 0`'s pattern as a variable, reduces `h 5`
# to 1 and refuses the module. When a re-sync brings upstream's fix, the
# reports, their PINS.md entries and this test go (upstream/README.md).
. "$IDRIS_MLIR_ROOT/tests/testutils.sh"
profile_accept .
